{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc 'for f in .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/001-workspace-skeleton-core-types-rng-and-saveload/20260315025033-spec.md .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/002-source-water-mixing-and-geometry-driven-thermal/20260315035345-spec.md .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/003-dissolved-pool-dynamics-do-model-ph-updates-and/20260315042843-spec.md; do echo \"FILE:$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,260p' \\\"\"'$f\"; echo; done'","aggregated_output":"FILE:.ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/001-workspace-skeleton-core-types-rng-and-saveload/20260315025033-spec.md\n---\nartifact: spec\nloop: 1\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: claude(opus)\nrole: planner\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T02:50:33Z\n---\n\n# Feature: Workspace Skeleton, Core Types, RNG, and Save/Load\n\n## Description\nBootstrap the Cargo workspace with all four crates (`tank_core`, `tank_data`, `tank_tui`, `tank_scenarios`), define the full domain type hierarchy (`TankState`, `TankGeometry`, `WaterState`, `PlayerAction`, `SimEvent`, `TankSnapshot`, etc.), implement the deterministic RNG wrapper using `ChaCha8Rng`, wire up JSON save/load with schema and app versioning, and establish the `SimulationEngine` trait with a minimal concrete implementation that can apply actions to a queue and step through empty ticks. This is Milestone 1 from the spec — the foundation every subsequent feature builds on.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cargo workspace compiles with four crates: `tank_core`, `tank_data`, `tank_tui`, `tank_scenarios`; `tank_core` has no TUI dependencies\n- [ ] `TankGeometry` struct is defined with all fields (`length_cm`, `width_cm`, `height_cm`, `fill_height_cm`, `glass_thickness_mm`, `open_top`) and derives `water_volume_l`, `surface_area_cm2`, `footprint_area_cm2`, `wall_area_cm2`, `mean_depth_cm`, `surface_area_to_volume_ratio`, `wall_area_to_volume_ratio`\n- [ ] `WaterState` stores all required dissolved pools as total amounts (`ammonia_total_mg_n_total`, `nitrite_mg_n_total`, `nitrate_mg_n_total`, `phosphate_mg_p_total`, `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total`, `dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total`, `dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c_total`, `dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total`, `alkalinity_meq_total`, and all 7 ion totals: Ca, Mg, Na, K, HCO3, Cl, SO4)\n- [ ] `TankSnapshot` derives all display values: `tan_mg_l`, `nh3_mg_l`, `nitrite_mg_l`, `nitrate_mg_l`, `phosphate_mg_l`, `do_mg_l`, `gh_d`, `kh_d`, `tds_mg_l`, `conductivity_us_cm`, `ph` using the exact formulas from the spec\n- [ ] `PlayerAction` enum defined with all 12 variants and validation logic that returns typed `SimError` (percentages in `0.0..=1.0` or `0.0..=100.0` as specified, non-negative grams/counts)\n- [ ] `SimEvent` struct with `day`, `hour`, `severity`, `kind`, `cause_codes`, `summary`; `EventKind` enum with all 13 required variants; `EventSeverity` enum (Info, Warning, Critical)\n- [ ] `SimSeed(u64)` wraps `ChaCha8Rng`; the RNG is stored in `TankState`; no thread-local RNG is used anywhere in `tank_core`\n- [ ] `SimulationEngine` trait implemented with `apply_action`, `step_hours`, `snapshot`, `full_state`; actions are queued and processed at the start of each hourly tick in insertion order\n- [ ] `TankState` contains all top-level sub-states: geometry, environment (ambient temp, hour-of-day, day counter), hardware (light, heater, filter, aeration), water, substrate layers, filter state, plant guild states, algae state, microbe state, microfauna state, animal (shrimp) state, detritus state, event log, and RNG\n- [ ] Save file is JSON containing: `schema_version`, `app_version`, full `TankState`, queued actions, and serialized RNG state\n- [ ] `save_load_roundtrip` test: create a state with a non-default seed, serialize to JSON, deserialize, and assert the restored state is identical (field-by-field equality)\n- [ ] `determinism_basic` test: two engines with the same seed stepping 24 hours produce identical snapshots\n- [ ] `action_validation` test: invalid actions (negative grams, out-of-range percentages, etc.) return `Err(SimError)` with descriptive variants\n- [ ] `action_queuing` test: multiple actions queued for the same tick are processed in insertion order\n- [ ] Invariant checks run after every `step_hours` call: no negative mass pools, no negative populations, index values clamped to `0.0..=1.0`, temperature above `0.0 C`\n- [ ] `tank_data` crate has TOML deserialization scaffolding with `serde` and `toml`; preset structs for source water, substrate, plant, and shrimp profiles are defined (loading actual preset files is included)\n- [ ] All preset TOML files created: source water (`soft_acidic`, `moderate`, `hard_shrimp`, `ro_like`), substrate (`inert_sand`, `inert_gravel`, `active_planted`, `coarse_porous`), plants (`fast_stem`, `root_rosette`), shrimp (`neocaridina_davidi`), process parameters (one default pack), and scenarios (`nano_cycle`, `medium_planted`, `warm_room`)\n- [ ] `open_top = false` stores a configurable lid factor (default `0.25`) that will reduce surface exchange rates when those systems are implemented\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `Cargo.toml` - Workspace root with members `crates/tank_core`, `crates/tank_data`, `crates/tank_tui`, `crates/tank_scenarios`\n- `crates/tank_core/Cargo.toml` - Dependencies: `serde`, `serde_json`, `rand`, `rand_chacha`, `thiserror`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/lib.rs` - Module re-exports\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/mod.rs` - Module declarations for all type modules\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/geometry.rs` - `TankGeometry` with derived calculations\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs` - `WaterState` with all dissolved pools\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/environment.rs` - `EnvironmentState` (ambient temp, time tracking)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs` - `LightState`, `HeaterState`, `FilterHardware`, `AerationState`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs` - `SubstrateLayerState`, `SubstrateKind`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs` - `PlantGuildState`, `AlgaeState`, `MicrobeState`, `MicrofaunaState`, `AnimalState` (shrimp), `DetritusState`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/events.rs` - `SimEvent`, `EventKind`, `EventSeverity`, `EventCause`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` - `TankSnapshot` with all derived display values and construction from `TankState`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs` - `PlayerAction` enum, validation, `SimError`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs` - `TankState` aggregate, `SimMeta`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/rng.rs` - `SimRng` wrapper around `ChaCha8Rng` with `SimSeed`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` - `SimulationEngine` trait and concrete `Engine` struct with action queuing, tick stepping, snapshot generation\n- `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs` - `SaveFile` struct, serialize/deserialize with schema version\n- `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs` - Post-tick invariant checking\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` - Save/load roundtrip test\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/determinism.rs` - Basic determinism test\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/validation.rs` - Action validation tests\n- `crates/tank_data/Cargo.toml` - Dependencies: `serde`, `toml`, `thiserror`\n- `crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs` - Preset loading and validation scaffolding\n- `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs` - Preset structs for source water, substrate, plants, shrimp, process params, scenarios\n- `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/soft_acidic.toml` - Soft acidic water preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/moderate.toml` - Moderate water preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/hard_shrimp.toml` - Hard shrimp water preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/ro_like.toml` - RO-like water preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/substrate/inert_sand.toml` - Inert sand preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/substrate/inert_gravel.toml` - Inert gravel preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/substrate/active_planted.toml` - Active planted substrate preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/substrate/coarse_porous.toml` - Coarse porous media preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/plants/fast_stem.toml` - Fast stem plant guild preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/plants/root_rosette.toml` - Root feeding rosette preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml` - Neocaridina davidi preset\n- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` - Default process parameters pack\n- `crates/tank_data/data/scenarios/nano_cycle.toml` - Nano cycling scenario\n- `crates/tank_data/data/scenarios/medium_planted.toml` - Medium planted scenario\n- `crates/tank_data/data/scenarios/warm_room.toml` - Warm room scenario\n- `crates/tank_tui/Cargo.toml` - Dependencies: `ratatui`, `crossterm`, `tank_core`\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs` - Placeholder module structure\n- `crates/tank_scenarios/Cargo.toml` - Dependencies: `tank_core`, `tank_data`\n- `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` - Placeholder module structure\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: none (this is the foundation)\n- Blocks: all subsequent features (geometry/temperature, dissolved pools, nitrogen cycle, substrate/plants, shrimp, TUI)\n\n---\n\nFILE:.ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/002-source-water-mixing-and-geometry-driven-thermal/20260315035345-spec.md\n---\nartifact: spec\nloop: 2\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: codex(gpt-5.4-xhigh)\nrole: planner\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T03:53:45Z\n---\n\nI’m reviewing `prompt.md`, the completed loop artifacts, and recent git checkpoints to determine what is already built and what the next unimplemented milestone should be.\nThe repo has no `loops/` directory in the working tree, so I’m pulling the relevant context from `spec.md`, the codebase, and the loop checkpoint commits instead.\nI’ve confirmed loop 1 built the workspace, preset loading, typed state, validation, RNG, save/load, and basic snapshot plumbing. I’m reading the engine and type implementations now to separate placeholders from real milestone-2 behavior.\nThe current code confirms milestone-2 behavior is not implemented yet: geometry math exists, but water changes are simple retention-only mass cuts and ambient temperature still assigns the room temperature directly without a heat model. I’m checking the loop artifacts next so the planned feature stays aligned with what was already approved.\nI’ve got the completed loop-1 artifacts now. The approved notes explicitly defer source-water chemistry mixing and heat-driven ambient response, which makes the next slice narrower than the original milestone name.\n# Feature: Source-Water Mixing and Geometry-Driven Thermal Response\n\n## Description\nLoop 1 already completed the workspace, deterministic state/RNG/save-load foundation, geometry helper math, snapshot derivations, preset-loading scaffolding, and the minimal queued-action engine. The next missing slice is to make those scaffolds causal: resolve scenario/source-water/process presets into runtime state, execute `WaterChangePercent` with real replacement chemistry and temperature instead of pure dilution, and update water temperature hourly from ambient air, heater settings, tank size, and lid exchange. This feature should explicitly exclude feed-to-TAN conversion, hourly DO consumption/reaeration, and broader cycling behavior for now; it exists to unlock correct water-change mass balance, ambient-temperature behavior, and the thermal half of tank-size response.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `TankState` gains runtime-resolved setup data needed for deterministic continuation: a stable in-state source-water catalog keyed by preset `id`, resolved process parameters, and any thermal observables required by tests; these fields serialize in save files and schema version is bumped if compatibility is broken.\n- [ ] `tank_scenarios::seeded_state` or a builder it delegates to materializes scenario presets into non-default state: scenario geometry populates `TankGeometry`, `environment.ambient_temp_c` comes from the scenario, initial `WaterState` totals come from the selected source-water profile multiplied by current fill volume, and substrate/plant state is derived from preset IDs instead of leaving `TankState::new` defaults in place.\n- [ ] Source-water presets stop using GH/KH/TDS summary values as hidden source-of-truth. Each preset carries explicit per-liter values for TAN, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, Ca, Mg, Na, K, HCO3, Cl, SO4, and temperature; loader validation rejects non-finite or negative chemistry and documents any derived-value tolerance.\n- [ ] `WaterChangePercent` removes exactly `percent / 100.0` of each tracked dissolved total, then adds replacement mass from the referenced source-water profile using exchanged liters. `0%` water changes are no-ops.\n- [ ] Water changes also mix water temperature by exchanged volume. Replacing `50%` of the tank with colder or warmer source water shifts `water.temperature_c` proportionally and does not jump to source temperature unless `percent = 100`.\n- [ ] Partial-failure invariant: if a queued water change references an unknown source profile or invalid resolved profile, `step_hours` returns a typed `SimError` and leaves `TankState`, queued actions, RNG state, `day`, `hour_of_day`, and `event_log` exactly unchanged. No partial mass removal, temperature mixing, or event emission is allowed.\n- [ ] The hourly temperature step uses the prompt’s discrete heat model with `dt_s = 3600.0`, `heat_capacity_j_per_k = volume_l * 4186.0`, `ua_total_w_per_k = (k_surface * surface_area_m2 * top_factor) + (k_wall * wall_area_m2)`, `q_ambient_w = ua_total_w_per_k * (ambient_temp_c - water_temp_c)`, heater output only when enabled and below `setpoint_c - deadband_c / 2.0`, and `delta_temp_c = (q_ambient_w + q_heater_w) * dt_s / heat_capacity_j_per_k`.\n- [ ] Existing geometry helpers drive the heat model. Smaller tanks respond faster than larger tanks, and `open_top = false` applies the existing lid multiplier to slow surface heat exchange relative to an open-top tank under the same conditions.\n- [ ] `ChangeAmbientTemperature` changes only `environment.ambient_temp_c`; water temperature changes gradually on later ticks. If ambient exceeds heater setpoint, heater output eventually becomes `0.0` and never goes negative.\n- [ ] A reusable `do_sat_mg_l` helper or observable is added using linear interpolation over `0 C -> 14.6`, `10 C -> 11.3`, `20 C -> 9.1`, `30 C -> 7.6`. Full DO mass updates remain out of scope for this feature, but the saturation target must be inspectable by tests and later systems.\n- [ ] `ro_like` acts as the zero-nutrient reference water for regression tests: a `50%` water change using it reduces `ammonia_total_mg_n_total`, `nitrite_mg_n_total`, `nitrate_mg_n_total`, `phosphate_mg_p_total`, `dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total`, and total tracked ions by `50% +/- 0.5%`.\n- [ ] Regression coverage is added for deterministic scenario materialization, `water_change_mass_balance`, `ambient_temperature_action`, and the thermal half of tank-size response (`10 L` reaches half of its eventual ambient-step delta in fewer than half as many ticks as `100 L`). The feed-pulse TAN half of `tank_size_response` remains blocked by later nitrogen-cycle work.\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/source_water.rs` - runtime source-water profile with per-liter chemistry and conversion helpers\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` - runtime process parameters for heat-transfer coefficients and later chemistry systems\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/mod.rs` - export new runtime setup types\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs` - persist resolved source-water catalog, process params, and thermal observables in `TankState`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs` - add initial-fill and water-change mixing helpers\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs` - expose last heater output or equivalent heater-runtime field\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` - surface thermal observables needed by tests and the future TUI\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs` - add typed lookup/resolution errors for water-change failures\n- `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs` - bump schema/version handling if expanded runtime state changes save compatibility\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/temperature.rs` - geometry-driven heat transfer and DO saturation target helper\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs` - exact source-water mixing logic and atomic application rules\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` - wire water-change and temperature systems into the hourly tick order\n- `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs` - expand `SourceWaterPreset` and `ProcessParamsPreset` schemas and validation\n- `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/*.toml` - explicit source-water chemistry, with `ro_like` as the zero-nutrient reference\n- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` - add heat-transfer coefficients used by the hourly model\n- `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` - build resolved `TankState` from scenario, source-water, substrate, plant, and process presets\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/water_change_mass_balance.rs` - exact water-change regression\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/ambient_temperature_action.rs` - gradual-warming and heater-cutoff regression\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/tank_size_thermal_response.rs` - geometry-dependent thermal response regression\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` - extend roundtrip coverage to include new runtime setup and thermal fields\n- `crates/tank_scenarios/tests/materialization.rs` - scenario-to-state resolution regression\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: Workspace Skeleton, Core Types, RNG, and Save/Load\n- Blocks: Nitrogen Cycle and Dissolved Oxygen Dynamics; full `tank_size_response`; scenario-backed manual play and later biology systems\n\n---\n\nFILE:.ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/003-dissolved-pool-dynamics-do-model-ph-updates-and/20260315042843-spec.md\n---\nartifact: spec\nloop: 3\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: claude(opus)\nrole: planner\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T04:28:43Z\n---\n\nNow I have a complete picture. Let me write the spec for Loop 3, which corresponds to Milestone 3.\n\n# Feature: Dissolved Pool Dynamics, DO Model, pH Updates, and Event Emission\n\n## Description\nImplement the hourly dissolved-pool update systems that make water chemistry dynamic. This loop adds: (1) light-state computation, (2) reaeration driving dissolved oxygen toward saturation, (3) background biological oxygen demand from existing biomass, (4) hourly pH/alkalinity/DIC updates so pH is no longer static, (5) NH3 speciation as a runtime utility usable during simulation (not just at snapshot time), and (6) threshold-based event emission for `AmmoniaWarning`, `NitriteWarning`, and `OxygenDip`. These systems form the foundation that Milestone 4 (decomposition, nitrification, cycling) will build upon. No nitrogen-cycle transformation (TAN→NO2→NO3) or detritus decomposition is included here — those belong to Loop 4.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A helper `is_light_on(hour_of_day: u8, photoperiod_hours: f64) -> bool` exists and is used in the hourly pipeline; light is centered on noon (hour 12), so an 8-hour photoperiod means hours 8–15 are lit\n- [ ] Reaeration system updates `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` each tick: `delta_do = kLa * (do_sat - do_mg_l) * volume_l * dt_h` where `dt_h = 1.0`, `kLa` scales with `top_exchange_factor` and aeration intensity\n- [ ] Background biological oxygen demand (BOD) is subtracted hourly: a small per-hour respiration draw proportional to total biomass (shrimp count, plant biomass, microbe biomass, algae biomass) so that DO can drop at night when photosynthesis is off\n- [ ] During lit hours, a small net photosynthetic O2 contribution is added from existing plant + periphyton biomass (simple proportional rate, not full plant-growth model — that is Loop 5)\n- [ ] DO is clamped to non-negative by the existing invariant system (no negative oxygen)\n- [ ] DIC and alkalinity are nudged hourly by a small background respiration/photosynthesis delta so pH drifts realistically (respiration adds DIC; photosynthesis during lit hours removes DIC)\n- [ ] pH is recomputed from alkalinity and DIC each tick using the existing `6.3 + log10(alk) - log10(dic)` formula, stored as `state.water.ph` (new field), so downstream systems can read it without recomputing\n- [ ] NH3 speciation helper `compute_nh3_mg_l(tan_mg_l, ph, temp_c) -> f64` exists in a shared location and is used by both the event emitter and `TankSnapshot`\n- [ ] After each hourly tick, event emission checks run:\n  - `AmmoniaWarning` if `nh3_mg_l >= 0.02` (with cause `HighAmmonia`)\n  - `NitriteWarning` if `nitrite_mg_l >= 0.5` (with cause `HighNitrite`)\n  - `OxygenDip` if `do_mg_l < 4.0` (with cause `LowOxygen`)\n  - Events are emitted at most once per day per kind to avoid log spam (track last-emitted day per kind)\n- [ ] `ProcessParams` is extended with new fields: `reaeration_kla_base`, `aeration_kla_boost`, `background_bod_mg_o2_per_g_biomass_per_hour`, `plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour`, `respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour`, `photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour`\n- [ ] Night oxygen dips are observable: a tank with plants and shrimp, run for 48 hours, shows lower DO at night hours than during the photoperiod\n- [ ] Aeration effect is observable: with aeration enabled at high intensity, DO recovers faster toward saturation than without\n- [ ] `save_load_resume` test still passes (new state fields serialize/deserialize correctly)\n- [ ] `determinism_same_seed` still holds (new systems are deterministic, no thread-local RNG)\n- [ ] All existing tests continue to pass\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/light.rs` — new file: `is_light_on` helper\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs` — new file: reaeration, BOD, photosynthetic O2\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` — new file: hourly pH/DIC/alkalinity update, `compute_nh3_mg_l` helper\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/events.rs` — new file: threshold-based event emission with daily dedup\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/mod.rs` — add `pub mod light; pub mod dissolved_oxygen; pub mod chemistry; pub mod events;`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` — extend `ProcessParams` with reaeration, BOD, and DIC rate fields\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs` — add `last_event_day: BTreeMap<String, u32>` (or similar) for daily dedup tracking\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs` — add `pub ph: f64` field to `WaterState`, initialize from DIC/alkalinity\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` — read `state.water.ph` instead of recomputing; use shared `compute_nh3_mg_l`\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` — wire new systems into `step_one_hour` at the correct pipeline positions (steps 5, 9, 10, 11-partial, 13)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs` — add pH range clamp (5.5..=8.5) to invariant checks\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/dissolved_oxygen.rs` — new test file: night dip test, aeration boost test, reaeration convergence\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/chemistry.rs` — new test file: pH drift test, NH3 speciation correctness\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs` — new test file: threshold emission, daily dedup, cause_codes non-empty\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: Loop 2 (geometry, temperature, water changes, DO saturation lookup)\n- Blocks: Loop 4 (decomposition + nitrification will consume O2, produce/consume alkalinity, and generate TAN that triggers AmmoniaWarning events)\n\n---\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
