- [x] `PlayerAction` enum with all 12 variants and validation returning typed `SimError` (percentages `0.0..=100.0`, fractions `0.0..=1.0`, non-negative grams, temperature > 0, non-empty source profile ID)\n- [x] `SimEvent` struct with `day`, `hour`, `severity`, `kind`, `cause_codes`, `summary`; `EventKind` enum with all 13 required variants; `EventSeverity` with Info/Warning/Critical\n- [x] `SimSeed(u64)` wraps `ChaCha8Rng` via `SimRng`; RNG stored in `TankState.rng`; no thread-local RNG in `tank_core`\n- [x] `SimulationEngine` trait implemented on `Engine` with `apply_action`, `step_hours`, `snapshot`, `full_state`; actions queued in `VecDeque` and drained in insertion order at start of each hourly tick\n- [x] `TankState` contains all top-level sub-states: geometry, environment, hardware (light/heater/filter/aeration), water, substrate layers, filter state, plant guild states, algae, microbe, microfauna, animal (shrimp), detritus, event log, RNG\n- [x] Save file is JSON containing `schema_version`, `app_version`, full `TankState`, `queued_actions`, and serialized RNG state (seed + draw count)\n- [x] `save_load_roundtrip` test: non-default seed (42), applies actions, steps 1 hour, serializes to JSON, deserializes, asserts field-by-field equality\n- [x] `determinism_basic` test: two engines with same seed (7) stepping 24 hours produce identical snapshots and full state\n- [x] `action_validation` test: negative grams → `NegativeValue`, percent 120 → `PercentOutOfRange`, fraction 1.1 → `FractionOutOfRange`, intensity -0.5 → `FractionOutOfRange`, intensity_index 1.2 → `FractionOutOfRange`, temperature 0.0 → `TemperatureTooLow`\n- [x] `action_queuing` test: RemoveShrimp(1) then AddShrimp(1) on 0 adults → result is 1 (proves insertion-order processing since reversed order would yield 0)\n- [x] Invariant checks run after every `step_hours`: non-negative mass pools, index values clamped `0.0..=1.0`, temperature > 0.0 C; event log trimmed to last 200\n- [x] `tank_data` has TOML deserialization via `serde`/`toml` with preset structs for source water, substrate, plant, shrimp, process params, and scenarios; presets loaded via `include_str!` compile-time embedding\n- [x] All preset TOML files created: source water (4), substrate (4), plants (2), shrimp (1), process params (1), scenarios (3) — all with `id`, `name`, parameters, and `[provenance]` blocks\n- [x] `open_top = false` stores configurable `lid_exchange_factor` (default `0.25`) via `TankGeometry.lid_exchange_factor` with `top_exchange_factor()` returning the factor when closed\n\n## Notes\n\nSolid Milestone 1 implementation. A few observations (none blocking):\n\n- **RNG serialization strategy**: Seed + draw-count replay is correct but O(n) on deserialization. Acceptable for v1 draw counts; the debug assertion at 2^32 draws provides a safety net.\n- **Water change dilution** correctly covers TAN, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, and all 7 ions — matching the future `water_change_mass_balance` test's required pools. DO is intentionally excluded (not required by that acceptance test).\n- **Source water mixing** and **temperature mixing** during water changes are acknowledged as deferred to Milestone 2. `ChangeAmbientTemperature` correctly sets `environment.ambient_temp_c` (not water temp), ready for the heat model.\n- Code is well-organized, consistently formatted, and `cargo test` passes cleanly across all 4 crates.\n\n## Commit Message\n\nfeat(tank-sim): milestone 1 — workspace skeleton, core types, RNG, save/load, and preset data\n\nFILE:.ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/002-source-water-mixing-and-geometry-driven-thermal/20260315042503-review-approved.md\n---\nartifact: review-approved\nloop: 2\niterations: 1\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: codex(gpt-5.4-high)\nrole: reviewer\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T04:25:03Z\n---\n\nReviewing the implementation against `prompt.md`, the loop-2 spec, and the current diff first. I’m enumerating the changed product files, reading 