I’m rerunning the test targets with both the Rust toolchain and linker on `PATH`.\nI have enough to close the review. I’m pulling exact line references for the approval evidence so the final review points to the concrete implementation and tests rather than summarizing loosely.\n# Review: APPROVED\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] Runtime-resolved source-water catalog and process params are persisted in `TankState`, and save compatibility was updated with schema version `2`.\n- [x] Scenario materialization now resolves geometry, ambient temperature, initial water chemistry, substrate layers, plant guilds, and the source-water catalog from presets deterministically.\n- [x] Source-water presets use explicit per-liter chemistry fields, loader validation rejects invalid values, and `ro_like` is the zero-nutrient regression reference.\n- [x] `WaterChangePercent` removes/adds dissolved totals by exchanged liters, mixes water temperature proportionally, and treats `0%` changes as a no-op.\n- [x] Unknown or invalid runtime source profiles fail atomically with typed errors before any queued action mutates state.\n- [x] The hourly temperature model uses geometry-driven heat exchange plus heater control, and `ChangeAmbientTemperature` only changes ambient air while water temperature responds through the heat model.\n- [x] `do_sat_mg_l` is implemented and exposed through snapshot observability together with heater output.\n- [x] Regression coverage exists for deterministic materialization, water-change mass balance, ambient-temperature behavior, thermal tank-size response, and save/load determinism.\n\n## Notes\nEvidence is in [state.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L19), [save.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/save.rs#L8), [presets.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs#L12), [lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs#L29), [source_water.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/source_water.rs#L27), [water.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs#L50), [water_change.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs#L6), [temperature.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/temperature.rs#L32), [engine.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs#L45), [snapshot.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs#L56), and [tank_scenarios/lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs#L59).\n\nRegression evidence is in [water_change_mass_balance.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/water_change_mass_balance.rs#L12), [ambient_temperature_action.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/ambient_temperature_action.rs#L15), [tank_size_thermal_response.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/tank_size_thermal_response.rs#L43), [save_load.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs#L28), and [materialization.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/tests/materialization.rs#L3).\n\nVerified by execution: `cargo test -p tank_core --tests` passed with 24 tests, and `cargo test -p tank_scenarios --tests` passed with 5 tests, using the Nix Rust/GCC toolchain available in the environment.\n\n## Commit Message\nImplement source-water mixing and geometry-driven thermal response\n\n---\n\nFILE:.ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/003-dissolved-pool-dynamics-do-model-ph-updates-and/20260315043901-review-approved.md\n---\nartifact: review-approved\nloop: 3\niterations: 0\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: claude(opus)\nrole: reviewer\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T04:39:01Z\n---\n\nAll 44 tests pass (0 failures). Here is the review:\n\n# Review: APPROVED\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] `is_light_on(hour_of_day, photoperiod_hours)` helper exists in `light.rs`, centered on noon (8h photoperiod = hours 8–15), used in engine pipeline\n- [x] Reaeration updates `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` each tick: `delta_do = kLa * (do_sat - do_mg_l) * volume_l` with `kLa` scaling by `top_exchange_factor` and aeration intensity\n- [x] Background BOD subtracted hourly proportional to total biomass (shrimp, plants, microbes, algae) via `respiring_biomass_g`\n- [x] During lit hours, net photosynthetic O2 contribution from plant + periphyton biomass scaled by light intensity\n- [x] DO clamped to non-negative by invariant system (`invariants.rs:4-6`)\n- [x] DIC and alkalinity nudged hourly by respiration/photosynthesis delta; alkalinity feedback proportional to net DIC change\n- [x] pH recomputed from alkalinity and DIC each tick using `6.3 + log10(alk) - log10(dic)` formula, stored as `state.water.ph`\n- [x] `compute_nh3_mg_l(tan_mg_l, ph, temp_c)` shared helper in `chemistry.rs`, used by both event emitter and `TankSnapshot`\n- [x] Event emission: `AmmoniaWarning` at nh3 >= 0.02 (HighAmmonia), `NitriteWarning` at nitrite >= 0.5 (HighNitrite), `OxygenDip` at DO < 4.0 (LowOxygen); deduped per day per kind via `last_event_day`\n- [x] `ProcessParams` extended with all 6 new fields: `reaeration_kla_base`, `aeration_kla_boost`, `background_bod_mg_o2_per_g_biomass_per_hour`, `plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour`, `respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour`, `photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour`\n- [x] Night oxygen dips observable: `dissolved_oxygen_dips_at_night_relative_to_lit_hours` test passes\n- [x] Aeration effect observable: `aeration_recovers_do_faster_than_passive_exchange` test passes\n- [x] `save_load_resume` test passes (new fields have `#[serde(default)]` for backward compat)\n- [x] `determinism_same_seed` holds (no thread-local RNG in new systems)\n- [x] All 44 existing + new tests pass with 0 failures\n\n## Notes\nClean implementation with well-structured separation of concerns. The decision to keep `ProcessParams::default()` neutral (DIC rates = 0.0) while the TOML preset activates them is a sound compatibility strategy that avoids breaking constructor-based tests while ensuring scenario-driven simulations exercise the full chemistry model. Pipeline ordering (steps 5, 9, 10, 13 before time advance) is correct per the spec.\n\n## Commit Message\nfeat(tank_core): add dissolved oxygen dynamics, hourly pH/DIC updates, light state, and threshold event emission (loop 3)\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
